We can think of DP: f(N) = maximum coins first player can obtain from N coins with optimal play. After move, opponent will then get f'(remaining) where now opponent becomes first player. Since zero-sum, the amount first player gets = max over moves of (coins taken in move + (remaining total - opponent's optimal from remaining)). Because total remaining after your move is N - taken. Opponent will get optimal from that remaining as first player; you will get the rest. So f(N) = max_{legal moves m} (taken_m + (N - taken_m - f(N - taken_m))) = max_{moves} (N - f(N - taken_m)). Since taken cancels: first term becomes N - f(N - taken). Thus f(N)= N - min_{legal moves} f(N - taken). So essentially you want to minimize opponent's optimal future.

